CursorWindow: MappedFile instead of mmap, sqlite JNI built for every host

Upstream: platform/frameworks/base commit a86bb7e464664498ab03bb320cd93957c3f8e2b7
  "Make sqlite JNI available for host Mac and Windows in libandroid_runtime"
  Author Michael Hoisie, 2025-08-05; committed 2025-08-08, merged into main
  2025-08-11. Change-Id I150fd216971cf486beda7c187945a758ebe5589c, Bug 317884162, 437248474.
  Roll-forward of the 2024 pair "Use MappedFile for mmap-related operations
  in CursorWindow" and "Enable SQLite JNI for host Mac and Windows", both
  reverted in October 2024, before android-16.0.0_r1.
  First tagged in android-16.0.0_r4 (not in r1, r2 or r3).
Diff fetched unchanged from
  https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/a86bb7e464664498ab03bb320cd93957c3f8e2b7%5E%21/
Needs 0002 (applies with line offsets only; afterwards the four changed
source files are byte-identical to the commit's versions).

Why: the official library (BLR2.250402.052) has this change. Evidence from
its x86_64 disassembly, against our x86_64 build of r1:
  * CursorWindow layout: every field after mAshmemFd sits 8 bytes later
    (CursorWindow::writeToParcel reads mData at 0x18 and the slot offsets
    at 0x38/0x3c; r1 has 0x10, 0x30/0x34): the added
    std::unique_ptr<MappedFile> mMappedFile member.
  * mmap/munmap: the official library has 17 direct mmap and 16 munmap call
    sites, ours 19 and 18. Matching the official mmap sites to ours by the
    strings around them leaves out exactly CursorWindow::maybeInflate and
    createFromParcel; after this commit those, and the munmap in
    ~CursorWindow and maybeInflate, go through MappedFile.
  * JNI: the CursorWindow table starts nativeCreate, nativeDispose,
    nativeCreateFromParcel, nativeWriteToParcel (r1: nativeCreate,
    nativeCreateFromParcel, nativeDispose, ...); with 0002 the whole table
    matches the official one.
On Linux the Android.bp and #ifdef __linux__ hunks select the same sources
and libraries as before; the behaviour change is limited to CursorWindow
memory mapping through android::base::MappedFile.
The follow-up c80d23f520 ("Add defensive empty checks to
CursorWindow.{writeTo,createFrom}Parcel") is not in the official library
(its writeToParcel has no mNumRows == 0 branch) and is not applied.

